  "limitations": "The module proves only selected-basis packaging: the explicitly selected transition determinant equals the finite product of the selected localized Smith coefficients, arbitrary equivalence choices give associated determinants, and the primitive integral product representative from the preceding module is associated with this selected determinant after localization. It does not identify that representative or determinant with historical R^(2), Hentzelt's module norm, a gcd of maximal minors or a determinantal ideal, a historical resultant, a normalized canonical or choice-independent value, or any later-stage R^(i) construction. No equation-(34) parallel R-product, primitive-descent strengthening, multiplicity theorem, or unbounded-tail result is asserted."
